  "id": "8ba2a058-0dc1-4020-b8be-5c3aea97a305",
  "type": "PARENT",
  "data": {
    "body": "A block of mass, $\\mathbf{M_1}$ = \\textbf{7 kg} that hangs freely from a non-stretchable string of negligible mass that runs over a pulley and is connected to another block of mass, $\\mathbf{M_2}$ = \\textbf{10.00 kg} that also hangs vertically down. The pulley can be modeled as a disk of mass \\textbf{m = 5 kg} and radius \\textbf{R = 0.5 m}. The rope does NOT slide over the surface of the pulley. Magnitude of acceleration due to gravity is $\\mathbf{g = 10   m/s^2}$. The pulley can be modeled as a disk ($I = \\frac{1}{2}mR^2$)",
    "numberingType": "NUMBER",
